From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: vc1: keep the bit reader slack inside sizeimage

The 16 KiB of slack the VC-1 bit reader needs past the end of a frame
was added to sizeimage each time the OUTPUT format was prepared, so
TRY_FMT and S_FMT with the format G_FMT returned grew it by 16 KiB
again, and negotiating the format did not converge.

Make the slack part of sizeimage instead of an addition to it: a VC-1
OUTPUT format is at least 1 KiB plus the slack and a larger size is
kept as it is, so preparing a format twice gives the same result. The
buffers of REQBUFS have sizeimage bytes and VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS uses the
size it is given unchanged, as the V4L2 API asks.

As userspace now decides how large the buffer is, refuse a frame that
does not leave the slack free at the end of its buffer.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h       |  5 +++++
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c   | 10 +++++++++-
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 10 ++++++----
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
index ec81dc10a..6fa169df2 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -39,6 +39,11 @@
 #define CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_MPEG4_DEC	BIT(8)
 
 #define CEDRUS_VC1_MIN_WIDTH		128
+/*
+ * Room the VC-1 bit reader needs in an OUTPUT buffer after the end of the
+ * frame. It is part of sizeimage and not available to the bitstream.
+ */
+#define CEDRUS_VC1_SRC_SLACK		SZ_16K
 
 /* The engine counts macroblock columns in 8 bits. */
 #define CEDRUS_MPEG4_MAX_WIDTH		4080
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 4025c57c1..1962c2047 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -556,6 +556,15 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	    picture->data_bit_offset > payload_bits - sc_offset)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/*
+	 * The bit reader over-reads past the end of the frame: the frame must
+	 * leave the slack that sizeimage includes free at the end of the buffer.
+	 */
+	buf_size = vb2_plane_size(src_buf, 0);
+	if (buf_size < CEDRUS_VC1_SRC_SLACK ||
+	    vb2_get_plane_payload(src_buf, 0) > buf_size - CEDRUS_VC1_SRC_SLACK)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* Decoded bitplanes must fit in the bitplanes control. */
 	if (picture->bitplane_flags &&
 	    cedrus_vc1_bitplane_size(ctx, run) > V4L2_VC1_BITPLANE_SIZE)
@@ -611,7 +620,6 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	 * Keep BITS_END_ADDR at the page-rounded allocation boundary as
 	 * a safety net against runaway DMA (watchdog timeout).
 	 */
-	buf_size = vb2_plane_size(src_buf, 0);
 	/*
 	 * Start the bit reader after the start code of an Advanced profile
 	 * buffer: with start-code detection enabled, reading over a start code
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 0e87f24f6..54a89d1ca 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -230,12 +230,14 @@ void cedrus_prepare_format(struct v4l2_pix_format *pix_fmt,
 		sizeimage = max_t(u32, SZ_1K, sizeimage);
 		/*
 		 * VC-1 over-reads the bitstream a little past the end of a frame
-		 * on the last macroblock; pad the source allocation so the bit
-		 * reader has slack and the DMA does not stall (see
-		 * cedrus_vc1_setup()).
+		 * on the last macroblock, so the source buffer needs slack for
+		 * the bit reader or the DMA stalls (see cedrus_vc1_setup()). The
+		 * slack is part of sizeimage, as a minimum: a format that is
+		 * read back and set again must not grow.
 		 */
 		if (pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE)
-			sizeimage += SZ_16K;
+			sizeimage = max_t(u32, SZ_1K + CEDRUS_VC1_SRC_SLACK,
+					  sizeimage);
 		/* The VP9 bitstream end address has a 1 KiB granularity. */
 		if (pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME)
 			sizeimage = ALIGN(sizeimage, SZ_1K);
